From 71a751995356ae231b722447cd5f923d3747684e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:14:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(render): the shadow sheet cache counts a component's
 style text once

Each ShadowRoot's entry kept its own copy of its <style> text and counted
it against the 8 MB bound, and every miss summed all entries again. A page
with many instances of one component spent the bound on copies (a 100 KB
component sheet: 80 instances remembered, the rest restyled on every
render) and paid a quadratic sum on its first render. Entries now share one
copy per distinct text, counted once and released with its last entry, and
the running total is kept instead of recomputed.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
